bench warrant.en:
A process issued by a presiding judge or by a court
   against a person guilty of some contempt, or indicted for some crime;
   -- so called in distinction from a justice's warrant.

bisulphide.en:
n. A sulphide having two atoms of sulphur in the molecule;
   a disulphide, as in iron pyrites, FeS2; -- less frequently called
   bisulphuret.

blow-off.en:
n. A blowing off steam, water, etc.;
adj. as, a blow-off cock or pipe.
adj. An outburst of temper or excitement.

borough-english.en:
n. A custom, as in some ancient boroughs, by which
   lands and tenements descend to the youngest son, instead of the eldest;
   or, if the owner have no issue, to the youngest brother.
